{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790283366,"nonce":"KO10h40bXUS1gBnolB1StpVz+EM=","message":"Revised 2026-09-24 (Luis), story-level, later the same day as comment #3 and superseding its second half. Design: doc/design/terminal-renderer.md.\n\nWhat stands from #3: saved views and flows are one thing, a flow does not return a render spec but calls a view, and a view call renders, handles interaction, writes its own edits through the host and blocks on the script's thread until the user quits.\n\nWhat changes:\n\n- Items are a jq query the view owns. Every view kind takes `query`, and the view runs it, re-runs it when the ref watcher (63c68d1) reports a change and after each of its own writes, keeping the cursor on the same id. There is no provider function and no static list; both were artefacts of the text, not decisions. What is given up is rows that are not issues.\n- The command is the spec. A view's input is one KWARGS object, the same object work.view.KIND(**kwargs) takes, so the input already is the serialization and {\"view\",\"bindings\",\"items\"} has nothing left to do. Nothing reads stdin, nothing prints a spec, `git work view` has no --format, --gui posts that object to the gui, and no TTY with no --gui is an error. An agent that wants data runs `git work issue PROGRAM`.\n- `pick=True` is removed: `flow pick ID` (9a24c8e) takes its id from the command line.\n- Actions injected into views are the deferred direction, replacing the on_change / on_select callback sketch: actions={\"Start\": start_fn} drawn as buttons on rows, cards and show, plus a global bar. A callback is an action the view invents a name for. work.view.split and questions to the user are deferred beside it.\n\nA saved view is therefore a flow whose function calls work.view.KIND with a query and the bindings it wants, and running it is `git work flow run NAME`.\n\nAffects f37603c (a saved view is that call), 52a2797 (package view keeps the kinds table as the argument contract; Spec and IsSpec go), 84dfbde (the terminal renderer, Bubble Tea v2, list and show first) and 8b06191 (--gui posts the KWARGS object).","files":null}]}